In September 2024, my team, Zenith Technologies, entered the SP Batey Hackathon with one problem in mind: families throw away food they forgot they had.

## Frésko

We designed Frésko in Figma: an app that tracks expiry dates, reads grocery receipts to add items for you, sends reminders before food goes off, and suggests recipes that use it up.

It reached the grand finals.

## The idea stayed

After the hackathon, the design sat in Figma while I finished my diploma, interned at Amber Creative and took on freelance work. But the idea kept coming back.

In April 2026 I started building it for real, on my own, and called it StillGood.

## Live

On 26 August 2026, StillGood went live on the Google Play Store. The core idea is the same as the hackathon design: know what's in your kitchen, use it before it goes off.
